(930716, 105840, 26930, '<td valign="top">First submission to the site :)<br/> <br/>I am very satisfied with the 88% I got in the first try :)<br/> <br/>Well, I am enjoying this site very much and I hope I can continue shooting amazing photos like this :)<br/> <br/>I have one in Complexity aswell :) Lets hope it does as good ;)</td>', 'First submission to the site :) I am very satisfied with the 88% I got in the first try :) Well, I am enjoying this site very much and I hope I can continue shooting amazing photos like this :) I have one in Complexity aswell :) Lets hope it does as good ;)', '2004-09-29 10:22:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(930740, 106114, 20673, '<td valign="top">I did not vote on this contest, but what a deserving winning photo!<br/>I adore this so much! You really captured the essence of a baby''s touch. CONGRATULATIONS on the win! You deserved it!</td>', 'I did not vote on this contest, but what a deserving winning photo!I adore this so much! You really captured the essence of a baby''s touch. CONGRATULATIONS on the win! You deserved it!', '2004-09-29 10:39:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(930741, 106710, 25404, '<td valign="top">Thankyou all for your comments and constructive criticisms,<br/>I agree that the glassware is distracting. <br/>I took a few shots with only the finger and candle, but this one had the best smoke and angle. <br/>I just ran out of time.  After about 30 goes without burning <br/>myself I didnt want to push my luck. <br/>I found myself starting to hold my finger there beyond the 1 second threshold in the interests of getting the right shot. It is easy to put a wet finger in the tip of a flame and not get burned.<br/>I was dipping my finger in water between shots and did not burn myself at all, the blackness is only the burning wax hitting water.<br/>The concern over whether I burned myself shows me <br/>that I achieved the desired effect of the viewer feeling the subject.<br/>So I was happy with my first DPchallenge entry on that score :-)</td>', 'Thankyou all for your comments and constructive criticisms,I agree that the glassware is distracting. I took a few shots with only the finger and candle, but this one had the best smoke and angle. I just ran out of time.  After about 30 goes without burning myself I didnt want to push my luck. I found myself starting to hold my finger there beyond the 1 second threshold in the interests of getting the right shot. It is easy to put a wet finger in the tip of a flame and not get burned.I was dipping my finger in water between shots and did not burn myself at all, the blackness is only the burning wax hitting water.The concern over whether I burned myself shows me that I achieved the desired effect of the viewer feeling the subject.So I was happy with my first DPchallenge entry on that score :-)', '2004-09-29 10:39:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(930750, 106612, 21245, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone who took the time to comment on my photo.  This is my second challange entry and it fared much better than my first.  It has been very encouraging to get such positive feedback!</td>', 'Thank you to everyone who took the time to comment on my photo.  This is my second challange entry and it fared much better than my first.  It has been very encouraging to get such positive feedback!', '2004-09-29 10:46:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(930758, 106824, 24642, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments, they really mean a lot to me.  This is my personal second best but it really means more to my than my PB because I put much more effort in it and I intended it to have a meaning, not just a pretty picture.  It really amazes me how differently voters look at this picture, some like it and some dislike it, I like that.<br/> <br/>Thanks again all of you and keep on commenting.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments, they really mean a lot to me.  This is my personal second best but it really means more to my than my PB because I put much more effort in it and I intended it to have a meaning, not just a pretty picture.  It really amazes me how differently voters look at this picture, some like it and some dislike it, I like that. Thanks again all of you and keep on commenting.', '2004-09-29 10:51:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(930761, 106965, 25873, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the comments.  I agree completely that the photo was not quite right - I was most disappointed with the blurry reflection.  This photo was a last minute shot (taken less than half and hour before the deadline) that I took because I was unhappy with my original idea.  I didn''t notice the blurriness till it was too late (I think it was caused by dustiness in the mirror!).</td>', 'Thank you for the comments.  I agree completely that the photo was not quite right - I was most disappointed with the blurry reflection.  This photo was a last minute shot (taken less than half and hour before the deadline) that I took because I was unhappy with my original idea.  I didn''t notice the blurriness till it was too late (I think it was caused by dustiness in the mirror!).', '2004-09-29 10:54:24.000000', NULL, 0),
